  "id": "COMPOUND:18496 - PROTEIN:5943",
  "verbalization": "Garcinone E is implicated in targeting multiple cellular pathways, with its effects ultimately leading to the inhibition of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP. This is supported by three distinct pathways, all of which converge on the enzyme through a series of intermediate targets. The first pathway involves Garcinone E targeting Raji cells, which are then inhibited by 3-(1H-Benzimidazol-2-Yl)-7-(Diethylamino)Chromen-2-One, a compound that itself targets LC-PTP. Similarly, Garcinone E also targets ZR-75-1, which is inhibited by another compound that also acts on LC-PTP. These findings suggest that Garcinone E may exert its effects through a mechanism that involves the inhibition of LC-PTP, possibly through a common pathway or a series of intermediate targets. The evidence indicates that Garcinone E is likely a modulator of LC-PTP activity, potentially through a mechanism that involves the inhibition of downstream targets that ultimately lead to the suppression of LC-PTP function.",
